WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.200
"How Bad Are Ultra-Processed Foods?"

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.400
At present, the United States
has the lowest life expectancy

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.200
of the top dozen
richest countries in the world.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.560
We also have the greatest share

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.040
of our diet composed
of ultra-processed foods.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.000
In fact, most of our diet.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.480
Most of what goes
into our mouth

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.160
isn’t considered real food.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.640
Could there be a connection?

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.360
Ultra-processed foods
are said to be troublesome

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.880
for a wide variety of reasons,

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.800
like all the packaging, etc.,

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.000
but I’m just going to discuss
the health aspects.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.160
Based on studies encompassing
nearly ten million participants,

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.720
greater exposure
to ultra-processed food

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.320
was associated
with a higher risk

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.120
of a variety
of adverse health outcomes,

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.920
including all-cause mortality,

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.680
meaning living
a significantly shorter life.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.160
As a reminder,
ultra-processed foods are,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.000
"Industrial formulations
of processed food substances

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.760
that contain little
or no whole foods

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.240
and typically include
flavorings, colorings,

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:06.880
emulsifiers,
and other cosmetic additives."

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.040
Think Twinkies.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.840
So, nutritionally vacuous
that you could go blind

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.480
from nutrient deficiencies
if that’s all you ate,

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.240
like this 14-year-old boy

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.240
who apparently lived
on French fries,

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.680
Pringles, white bread,
ham, and sausage.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.600
Some of the health outcomes
make sense,

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:28.080
like higher ultra-processed
food consumption

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.680
being associated with more
dental cavities in kids.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.640
That makes sense since a lot
of them are packed with sugar.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.200
Higher ultra-processed
food consumption

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.120
is also associated
with an increased risk

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.480
of high blood pressure.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.240
That makes sense as a lot
of them are packed with salt.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.760
And with high blood pressures,
you can see

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:48.640
how there can be a higher rate
of cardiovascular events

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:49.920
like heart attacks and strokes.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.000
And since
cardiovascular diseases

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.440
are our leading killers,

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.040
you can see how that could lead
to increased overall mortality.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.960
Obesity is also a no-brainer.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:00.400
A lot of ultra-processed
products

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.080
are packed with calories,

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.240
and furthermore
intentionally engineered

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.000
with hyperpalatable combinations
of fat, sugar, salt, and flavors

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.120
so you can’t just eat one,
promoting weight gain

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.040
through so-called
hedonic eating,

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.160
meaning eating for pleasure

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.280
even if you aren’t
really hungry.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:18.160
I can see all that,

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:23.360
but why would there also
be a higher overall cancer risk

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.280
associated with ultra-processed
food consumption?

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.040
Or a higher risk of dementia?

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.240
Or a higher risk
of inflammatory bowel disease?

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.920
Or a higher risk
of irritable bowel syndrome?

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:39.200
And a higher risk of developing
chronic kidney disease, too?

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.000
Overall, direct associations
have been found

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.840
between exposure
to ultra-processed foods

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.000
and 70%
of the health issues

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.000
that were investigated.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.240
A higher risk of dying
from all causes put together,

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:52.880
a higher risk of getting cancer,
not sleeping well,

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.240
suffering from anxiety,
depression,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.920
and other common
mental disorders,

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.680
wheezing,
cardiovascular disease,

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.280
Crohn’s disease,
abdominal obesity,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.760
obesity in general,
fatty liver disease,

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.280
type 2 diabetes.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.440
So, increased risk of a variety

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.400
of chronic diseases
and mental health disorders.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.640
And apparently
not a single study

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.520
reported an association between
ultra-processed food intake

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.920
and beneficial health outcomes.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.280
There was never a,

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.640
"Take two Twinkies
and call me in the morning."

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.640
Given the large body of evidence

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.200
implicating ultra-processed
foods in human diseases,

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.000
and their ever-increasing
consumption around the world,

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.120
there is a pressing need
to recognize their contribution

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:34.560
to the global burden of disease.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.400
All right, but wait.
These are associations.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.640
Just because A
is correlated with B

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:43.120
doesn’t mean that A causes B.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.640
Maybe B causes A.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.680
For example,
snapshot-in-time studies show

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.520
that intake of higher
ultra-processed foods

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.120
is associated
with increased odds

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.440
of depression
or anxiety symptoms,

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:56.560
but individuals might turn
to ultra-processed foods

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:00.080
in an attempt to mitigate
stress-related anxiety.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:03.920
They don’t call it
comfort food for nothin’.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.320
Now there are
longitudinal studies

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.400
showing that greater intake
of ultra-processed foods

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.080
preceded depression,

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.720
but maybe the food was just used
to fend off bad feelings

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:15.760
for years before
any official diagnosis.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:19.200
But reverse causation,
B causing A,

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.520
seems less plausible
when it comes

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.000
to non-mental health outcomes.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.160
For example, it’s harder
to paint a picture

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.600
of how a heart attack
would cause people to then go on

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.480
to eat more junk food
instead of vice versa.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:35.280
The other big issue when trying
to establish cause-and-effect

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.080
from observational,
correlational data

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.160
is confounding.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:42.640
Maybe the reason A
is associated with B

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:46.320
is that some
third confounding factor, C,

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.600
is linked to both.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.600
For example, if people
who eat more junk

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.840
tend to smoke more,

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.720
no wonder junk eaters
would be dying more,

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:56.400
but it would have more
to do with the cigarettes

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.480
they put in their mouth
rather than the food.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.120
And indeed,
people consuming unhealthy diets

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:04.960
are also likely to smoke, drink,
and not exercise,

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:08.320
but we have ways to control
for these factors.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.840
Indeed, the majority
of studies

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.240
were adjusted
for these confounders.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.560
The most obvious
confounding factor, though,

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:16.000
is that highly processed foods

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.160
just tend to be more
likely to be junky crap.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.080
The reason cakes, crullers,
candy, and cola are bad for us

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:26.400
may have less to do
with how much they’re processed

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.360
and more to do
with the fact

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.480
that they are cakes,
crullers, candy, and cola,

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:31.920
packed with sugar
and calories,

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:34.000
with very few nutrients.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.760
Diets high
in ultra-processed foods

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.160
are diets high in added sugars,
saturated fat,

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.600
sodium, and calories,

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.280
displacing more
nutritious foods,

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.520
such as fruits, vegetables,
legumes, nuts, and seeds.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:45.040
So, maybe ultra-processed foods

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.760
are just markers
of poor diet quality.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.400
And indeed, the more
ultra-processed foods people eat

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.840
the more refined carbs
they’re eating,

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.560
the more sugar, saturated fat,
sodium, energy, cholesterol,

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:57.440
and the less fiber
in their diets.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.600
So, where’s the mystery?

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:03.200
People who eat more bad foods
get more diseases.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.280
We already knew that.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:09.440
What does processing
per se have to do with it?

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.440
Because ultra-processed
category foods

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:13.520
are more likely
to be crappy foods,

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:16.080
we could use it
as a kind of heuristic

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.400
that they probably
won’t be good for us.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.440
For example,
if you made up some rule

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.680
that you’re going to avoid
breakfast cereals

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:27.760
with cartoon characters on them,
you’d probably end up healthier,

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.560
but not because the graven image
of Tony the Tiger

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.800
magically hastens you
to the grave,

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:37.520
but rather because they’re
proxies for high sugar content.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:41.440
But for the developers
of the ultra-processed concept,

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:44.240
"ultra-processed" was no proxy.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.880
They claimed that
the harmful effects

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.920
of ultra-processed foods
are not fully captured

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:53.920
by their nutrient profile,
and even go as far to say

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.680
we should avoid
ultra-processed foods,

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:59.120
irrespective
of their nutrient profiles.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:02.000
Whether ultra-processed diets
are detrimental to health

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.240
simply because they are
of a poor nutritional quality,

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:07.760
or whether the nature
and extent of processing itself

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:11.120
has health consequences
has been an ongoing debate.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:14.880
How might we settle it?

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.240
Well, if it were the case

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.240
that the association between
ultra-processed foods

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.320
and poor health was solely
because

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:22.880
of the excess saturated fat,
sugar, and salt,

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.640
or just from a less healthful
dietary pattern in general,

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:30.400
then, if we were to adjust
for dietary quality,

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.080
the association between
ultra-processed foods

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.080
and disease should disappear.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.480
In other words, if it was
all about the nutrients,

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:38.240
then people eating crappy diets

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:40.000
high in saturated fat,
salt, and sugar

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.720
should have high disease rates
regardless of whether they eat

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:45.040
more ultra-processed foods
or less of them.

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:46.960
And people who eat
really healthy diets

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:49.280
should have low rates
of disease regardless

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.000
of how many ultra-processed
foods they consume.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.960
But that’s not the case.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:59.040
The majority of the associations
between ultra-processed foods

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:03.360
and obesity and health problems
remain significant and unchanged

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:08.320
in magnitude after adjustment
for diet quality or pattern.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:11.440
Meaning, even if you balance out
dietary quality,

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:12.960
those eating more
ultra-processed

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:15.120
tend to do worse.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.920
This suggests that at least
some of the adverse consequences

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:19.360
of ultra-processed foods

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:22.160
are independent
of dietary quality,

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:23.040
so it’s not as though

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.640
the ultra-processed
food companies

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:26.560
can just reformulate
their products

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.600
to be lower in salt or sugar
and be done with it.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:32.880
There appears to be something
about this class of foods

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:35.120
beyond the standard
nutrient profile

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:37.840
that contributes
to their deleterious effects.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:40.480
And that’s just what
I’ll be discussing

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:45.924
in this extended video series
on ultra-processed foods.

